<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Conrad of Montferrat</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1146–1192</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Conrad of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/montferrat">Montferrat</a> was an Italian nobleman who arrived at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tyre">Tyre</a> in 1187 and held it against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saladin">Saladin</a> after the fall of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a>. He became Marquis of Montferrat and, through marriage to Isabella, claimant to the crown of Jerusalem, and was elected king in April 1192. Days later he was murdered in Tyre by two <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nizari-ismailism">Nizari</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/order-of-assassins">Assassins</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/conrad-of-montferrat.jpg" alt="Conrad of Montferrat" width="320" height="571" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: AnonymousUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:IsabelaKOnrad.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
